capability list/compact  a list with each run of equal neighbours reduced to its first
  heroes  lists.compact
  go      slices.Compact, slices.CompactFunc
  rust    Vec::dedup, Vec::dedup_by, Vec::dedup_by_key, slice::partition_dedup, slice::partition_dedup_by, slice::partition_dedup_by_key
  python  -
  note    Go and Rust disagree where the equality is not transitive: Go compares each element with its neighbour, Rust with the last one kept, so two numbers at most one apart compact [1, 2, 3, 4, 10] to [1, 10] in Go and [1, 3, 10] in Rust, observed. Go's is taken, so `compact` keeps the first element of each run `lists.runs_by` answers

