  heroes  refused: needs a generic record
  go      -
  rust    slice::split_at, slice::split_at_checked, slice::split_first, slice::split_last, slice::split_first_chunk, slice::split_last_chunk, slice::split_off, slice::split_off_first, slice::split_off_last, slice::split_once, slice::rsplit_once, slice::shift_left, slice::shift_right, Vec::split_off, Vec::pop, Vec::pop_if
  python  list.pop
  note    the two parts are `lists.take` and `lists.skip`; a pop is `lists.last` and `lists.skip_last`

capability list/endless  a sequence with no end
  heroes  refused: a list is whole in memory, so one with no end cannot be said
  go      -
  rust    Iterator::cycle
  python  itertools.count, itertools.cycle
  note    so many of them are `range` and `lists.cycle`

## dropped

# Plumbing, with its reason. Nothing here is a thing a program does to a list.

dropped capacity  a list's capacity is the runtime's, and no program states it
  go      slices.Clip, slices.Grow
